@startuml reservation-saga-sequence
title Reservation saga — confirmation, hold rejection and payment compensation
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
skinparam wrapWidth 420
autonumber

participant "booking-service" as Booking
participant "orchestrator-service\nSagaCoordinator + strategies" as Saga
participant "inventory-service\nSeatHoldService" as Inventory
participant "payment-service\nPaymentService" as Payment

legend left
  ->> = asynchronous command/event through RabbitMQ (Docker Compose).
  Each arrow abbreviates: committed outbox → relay → ticketing exchange → destination queue.
  TX = one local database transaction: inbox claim + business changes + outbound outbox.
  Booking uses a local transaction and status guards, without an inbox.
endlegend

note over Booking,Payment
  Entry: Booking has committed Reservation(PENDING) + outbox ReservationRequested.
  Creation details: reservation-flow-sequence.puml.
  All messages carry reservationId and correlationId. Databases are separate.
end note
Booking ->> Saga: ReservationRequested\nreservation.requested → orchestrator.queue
Saga -> Saga: ReservationRequestedStrategy::handle()\nTX: create Saga(AWAITING_SEATS) + outbox HoldSeats; COMMIT
Saga ->> Inventory: HoldSeats\nseats.hold → inventory.queue
Inventory -> Inventory: HoldSeatsHandler → hold()\nTX: validate show and seat IDs; SeatLockingService::attemptHold()
note right of Inventory
  Sorted seat IDs; PESSIMISTIC_WRITE on seat rows.
  Check all requested seats before changing any.
end note

alt Hold rejected: missing show/seats or seats unavailable
    Inventory -> Inventory: TX: outbox SeatHoldRejected(reason); COMMIT\nNo seats held for this request
    Inventory ->> Saga: SeatHoldRejected\nseats.hold_rejected → orchestrator.queue
    Saga -> Saga: SeatHoldRejectedStrategy::handle()\nTX: AWAITING_SEATS → CANCELLED, recordFailure(reason)\n+ outbox ReservationCancelled; COMMIT
    Saga ->> Booking: ReservationCancelled\nreservation.cancelled → booking.queue
    Booking -> Booking: ReservationCancelledHandler\n→ ReservationCancellationService::onReservationCancelled()\nTX: PENDING → CANCELLED; COMMIT
else Hold succeeds
    Inventory -> Inventory: TX: seats AVAILABLE → HELD; persist SeatHold(expiresAt)\n+ outbox SeatsHeld; COMMIT
    Inventory ->> Saga: SeatsHeld\nseats.held → orchestrator.queue
    Saga -> Saga: SeatsHeldStrategy::handle()\nTX: AWAITING_SEATS → AWAITING_PAYMENT\n+ outbox ProcessPayment; COMMIT
    note left of Saga
      Amount, currency and paymentMethodToken currently
      come from SeatsHeldStrategy configuration defaults.
    end note
    Saga ->> Payment: ProcessPayment\npayment.process → payment.queue
    Payment -> Payment: ProcessPaymentHandler → process()\nTX: create/reuse Payment; FakePaymentGateway::process()\nGateway request idempotencyKey = reservationId
    note right of Payment
      Current gateway is local FakePaymentGateway.
      tok_decline produces PAYMENT_DECLINED;
      other tokens succeed. No real provider call.
    end note

    alt Payment succeeds
        Payment -> Payment: TX: Payment → PAID + outbox PaymentSucceeded; COMMIT
        Payment ->> Saga: PaymentSucceeded\npayment.succeeded → orchestrator.queue
        Saga -> Saga: PaymentSucceededStrategy::handle()\nTX: AWAITING_PAYMENT → PAYMENT_PAID\n+ outbox ConfirmSeats; COMMIT
        Saga ->> Inventory: ConfirmSeats\nseats.confirm → inventory.queue
        Inventory -> Inventory: ConfirmSeatsHandler → confirm()\nTX: check active hold; lock seats held by this reservation\nSeats HELD → SOLD, SeatHold → CONFIRMED\n+ outbox SeatsConfirmed; COMMIT
        Inventory ->> Saga: SeatsConfirmed\nseats.confirmed → orchestrator.queue
        Saga -> Saga: SeatsConfirmedStrategy::handle()\nTX: PAYMENT_PAID → CONFIRMED\n+ outbox ReservationConfirmed; COMMIT
        Saga ->> Booking: ReservationConfirmed\nreservation.confirmed → booking.queue
        Booking -> Booking: ReservationConfirmedHandler\n→ ReservationConfirmationService::onReservationConfirmed()\nTX: Reservation → CONFIRMED; COMMIT
    else Payment fails
        Payment -> Payment: TX: Payment → FAILED + outbox PaymentFailed(reason); COMMIT
        Payment ->> Saga: PaymentFailed\npayment.failed → orchestrator.queue
        Saga -> Saga: PaymentFailedStrategy::handle()\nTX: AWAITING_PAYMENT → COMPENSATING, recordFailure(reason)\n+ outbox ReleaseSeats; COMMIT
        Saga ->> Inventory: ReleaseSeats\nseats.release → inventory.queue
        Inventory -> Inventory: ReleaseSeatsHandler → release()\nTX: check active hold; lock seats held by this reservation\nSeats HELD → AVAILABLE, SeatHold → RELEASED\n+ outbox SeatsReleased; COMMIT
        Inventory ->> Saga: SeatsReleased\nseats.released → orchestrator.queue
        Saga -> Saga: SeatsReleasedStrategy::handle()\nTX: COMPENSATING → CANCELLED\n+ outbox ReservationCancelled; COMMIT
        Saga ->> Booking: ReservationCancelled\nreservation.cancelled → booking.queue
        Booking -> Booking: ReservationCancelledHandler\n→ ReservationCancellationService::onReservationCancelled()\nTX: PENDING → CANCELLED; COMMIT
        note over Saga,Inventory
          Compensation is a new committed operation that releases seats.
          It does not roll back earlier transactions across services.
        end note
    end
end

note over Booking,Payment
  Delivery is at least once. Inventory, Payment and Orchestrator deduplicate message_id via inbox.
  Messenger handlers call SagaCoordinator::handle(), which selects an automatically registered strategy.
  SagaExecutor locks existing saga rows, checks Workflow::can(), applies the transition and runs the reaction.
  Missing saga / disallowed transitions are no-ops. Booking ignores repeated terminal updates.
end note
note over Saga,Inventory
  Confirm/release paths above assume an active hold and seats owned by the reservation.
  If those checks fail, current code returns without a completion event;
  the saga may remain PAYMENT_PAID / COMPENSATING. No recovery path is invented here.
  expiresAt is stored, but expiry scheduling and compensation are not implemented.
end note
@enduml
